## 2. Data — CC BY-NC-SA 4.0

The analysis is built on the **Brazilian E-Commerce Public Dataset by Olist**, published on
Kaggle at `olistbr/brazilian-ecommerce` under
**[Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/)**.

That licence governs the source data **and every file derived from it**, which in this
repository means:

- `data/processed/fact_orders.csv`
- `data/processed/dq_issue_log.csv`
- `data/processed/query_outputs/*.csv`
- `dashboard/data/dashboard_data.js`
- `excel/delivery_sla_olist_marketplace.xlsx`
- every figure quoted in `reports/` and `docs/`

The raw dataset itself is **not** redistributed here — `data/external/` is excluded from
version control, and `database/fetch_data.py` downloads it from Kaggle on demand.

### What the data licence requires of you

| Term | What it means here |
|---|---|
| **BY** — Attribution | Credit Olist as the source and link the licence. Do not imply Olist endorses this analysis. |
| **NC** — NonCommercial | You may not use the data, or anything derived from it, for commercial purposes. |
| **SA** — ShareAlike | If you remix or build on the derived data, distribute your version under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 too. |

The MIT licence in section 1 does **not** override any of this. You may reuse the code
commercially; you may not reuse the data or the derived outputs commercially.

### Attribution

> Brazilian E-Commerce Public Dataset by Olist, available at
> https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/olistbr/brazilian-ecommerce,
> licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

